definitionOfDone:
The three decoders accept the exact shapes and return detached copies. Each malformed variant returns null, in table-driven vitest cases:
- an extra or missing key;
- a wrong type;
- a short or non-hex commit;
- a negative or unsafe integer;
- an unknown status or decision;
- reasons or changedPaths over the cap.

completionSummary:
CQ-C07a: daemon-owned plan-reuse state contract. It adds no decision logic.
- schema.ts: adds PlanSourceBasis, PlanningEntry, PlanReuseDecision and PlanReuseRecord, plus optional Task fields planSourceBasis, planningEntry and planReuse, documented as daemon-owned and never approval, readiness or evidence.
- context/planReuseState.ts (new):
  - three never-throwing readers: exact enumerable key-set check, each field read once, detached copies;
  - validatePlanReuseRecord, which throws only INVALID_INPUT;
  - capturePlanSourceBasis: openProjectGit with a 2000 ms budget, then rev-parse --verify --end-of-options HEAD^{commit}; null on any failure;
  - the planSourceGit seam.
- taskStore.updateTask:
  - strips all three fields from caller updates;
  - takes daemonOwned planSourceBasis{commit} and planReuse, both validated before any write;
  - a PLAN_SUBMITTED+daemonOwned write sets the basis {version 1, commit, this write's planRevision} or deletes it;
  - a status change into PLANNING stamps planningEntry {from, at = updatedAt, seq+1, wraps at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER}. The exception: the stored row is BLOCKED with blockedFromStatus PLANNING.
- WebSocketServer: UPDATE_TASK_DENYLIST lists the three keys.
- submitPlan: captures the basis once per call, outside the mutex; the cached-path retry reuses it; a null capture never refuses or warns.
- executionContract.test.ts: the race test is now order-agnostic (planned).
Tests: planReuseState.test.ts (117 cases: decoder tables, named stamp cases, ownership/refusal, real-Git submit cases) and a WS spy case.
SIZE NOTE for QA: the task's diff is 418 raw net lines (edited files +101, new files 116+201), about 355 excluding blank and comment lines. About 220 of them are DoD-mandated table-driven tests. I compacted it from 449 without dropping any case. It is still over the 400 default: please judge on substance or ask the architect.
